::U6F3_01::Nicotine can {=produce dependence and withdrawal ~guarantee focus ~remove lung risk ~reverse THC}

::U6F3_02::Vape emissions are {=aerosol, not harmless water vapor ~oxygen only ~always nicotine-free ~clean air}

::U6F3_03::Dual use means {=using cigarettes and e-cigarettes ~quitting ~using two flavors ~safe use}

::U6F3_04::THC may impair {=attention, memory, reaction time, coordination, and judgment ~only price recognition ~only packaging ~no safety skill}

::U6F3_05::Delayed effects increase risk when {=a person takes more before the first amount fully affects them ~they eliminate impairment ~they verify potency ~they guarantee medical use}

::U6F3_06::Natural or legal {=does not automatically mean harmless ~guarantees safe driving ~prevents dependence ~proves marketing}

::U6F3_07::Social-media visibility {=does not prove most people use ~is prevalence data ~proves safety ~eliminates bias}

::U6F3_08::Evaluate marketing by {=checking composition, evidence, missing context, and source credibility ~counting likes ~testing the product ~trusting colors}
